{"updated":"2023-03-07T05:34:43.475482+00:00","uuid":"05afc62c-23c2-468f-8dea-954e6c09bbfc","created":"2009-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","revision_id":88,"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/0905.3500?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/0905.3500?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/0905.3500?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/0905.3500?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/0905.3500?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/0905.3500?format=cv"},"id":"0905.3500","metadata":{"citation_count_without_self_citations":148,"publication_info":[{"year":2009,"artid":"013","page_start":"013","journal_title":"JCAP","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1212538"},"journal_volume":"07"}],"citation_count":152,"core":true,"dois":[{"value":"10.1088/1475-7516/2009/07/013"}],"titles":[{"title":"Density fluctuations from warm inflation"},{"title":"Density fluctuations from warm inflation","source":"arXiv"}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","authors":[{"uuid":"333bb4a6-1425-467b-9edd-1148d216053c","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/2523876"},"full_name":"Graham, Chris","affiliations":[{"value":"Newcastle upon Tyne U.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903580"}}],"signature_block":"GRANc"},{"uuid":"7c160762-56da-4f77-9064-58e997d7a30e","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/996694"},"full_name":"Moss, Ian G.","affiliations":[{"value":"Newcastle upon Tyne U.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903580"}}],"signature_block":"Mi"}],"curated":true,"figures":[{"key":"ccc418ffb10e671aaaaf37433913bac6","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/ccc418ffb10e671aaaaf37433913bac6","source":"arxiv","caption":"The time evolution of the inflaton perturbation for several runs with $c=1$ and $r=5$ is shown on the left. The histogram on the right shows the values of the inflaton perturbation athorizon crossing ($z=-1$) for $10000$ runs.","filename":"plots_fig1a.png"},{"key":"350e25d89086931d151e0bd577b97665","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/350e25d89086931d151e0bd577b97665","source":"arxiv","caption":"The time evolution of the inflaton perturbation for several runs with $c=1$ and $r=5$ is shown on the left. The histogram on the right shows the values of the inflaton perturbation athorizon crossing ($z=-1$) for $10000$ runs.","filename":"plots_fig1b.png"},{"key":"6ba8146580849c98a6a8bce19b709271","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/6ba8146580849c98a6a8bce19b709271","source":"arxiv","caption":"The variance of the inflaton at horizon exit from the numerical simulations has been plotted against $r=\\Gamma/3H$ for $c=0$ ($\\Gamma$ independent of $T$). The data are averages over$1000$ runs. The curve shows the approximation Eq. (\\ref{yapprox}).","filename":"plots_fig4.png"},{"key":"589aebd5f9f26880cfc6e4652973f8e3","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/589aebd5f9f26880cfc6e4652973f8e3","source":"arxiv","caption":"The variance of the inflaton at horizon exit from the numerical simulations has been plotted against $r=\\Gamma/3H$ for $c=1$ ($\\Gamma\\propto T$). The data are averages over $1000$ runs. The curve shows the numerical fit$A_1r^{5/2}+B_1r^{3/2}$.","filename":"plots_fig2.png"},{"key":"fc32b4e0ccfff9707a81eb4e80715daa","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/fc32b4e0ccfff9707a81eb4e80715daa","source":"arxiv","caption":"The variance of the inflaton at horizon exit from the numerical simulations has been plotted against $r=\\Gamma/3H$ for $c=-1$ ($\\Gamma\\propto T^{-1}$). The data are averages $1000$ runs. The curve shows the numerical fit$A_{-1}r^{-2}+B_{-1}r^{-3}$.","filename":"plots_fig6.png"}],"texkeys":["Graham:2009bf"],"citeable":true,"keywords":[{"value":"fluctuation: thermal","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"density: perturbation","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"inflaton: fluctuation","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"inflation","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"temperature dependence","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"power spectrum","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"numerical calculations","schema":"INSPIRE"}],"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"Thermal fluctuations provide the main source of large scale density perturbations in warm inflationary models of the early universe. For the first time, general results are obtained for the power spectrum in the case when the friction coefficient in the inflaton equation of motion depends on temperature. A large increase in the amplitude of perturbations occurs when the friction coefficient increases with temperature. This has to be taken into account when constructing models of warm inflation. New results are also given for the thermal fluctuations in the weak regime of warm inflation when the friction coefficient is relatively small.","source":"arXiv"}],"references":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/154280"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"347","page_start":"347","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D","journal_volume":"23"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/36357"},"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"hep-ph/9311278","publication_info":{"artid":"2441","page_start":"2441","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D","journal_volume":"50"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/468350"},"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"hep-ph/9803394","publication_info":{"artid":"123508","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D","journal_volume":"58"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/793032"},"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"0808.1855","publication_info":{"artid":"026901","journal_title":"Rept.Prog.Phys.","journal_volume":"72"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/617947"},"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"astro-ph/0305015","publication_info":{"artid":"083525","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D","journal_volum